course: dictionary
lesson: 13995
title: Loquat
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A loquat is a small, round fruit with orange-yellow skin. It tastes sweet with a little sour, and it has big brown seeds inside.
explain: The word loquat can also mean the tree that the fruit grows on. «We picked loquats from the tree in the garden.» Here loquats means the fruit, because you pick fruit, not a whole tree.
explain: «The loquat tree stayed green all winter.» Here the tree is the meaning, because a tree stays green, not a fruit. Read the words around the word to decide which meaning fits.
fact: A loquat is a small, round fruit that is orange-yellow.
fact: Loquats taste sweet with a little sour, and they have big brown seeds.
fact: Loquats first came from China.
fact: Loquats grow in warm places such as Australia, New Zealand, California and Mediterranean countries.
fact: Evergreen means a tree keeps its leaves all year round.
exercise: «We ate a juicy loquat at the picnic.» What is a loquat? | *A small, round, orange-yellow fruit | A large green vegetable | A cold drink made from milk | A type of bird
exercise: Where did loquats first come from? | Iceland | Norway | Peru | *China
exercise: Which of these is a warm place where loquats grow? | Greenland | *Australia | Iceland | Norway
test: Which words describe a loquat's taste? | Hot and spicy | Salty and bitter | Crunchy like a nut | *Sweet with a little sour
test: What does evergreen mean for a tree? | It has pink flowers every spring | *It keeps its leaves all year round | It loses all its leaves in autumn | It grows only in water
exam: «We picked loquats from the tree.» In this sentence, what does loquats mean? | A bird that sits in the tree | The wood of the tree | *The fruit you can eat | The leaves of the tree
